n a  country's finances  or on the rights of local communities  for years to come  the dependencies this can create  directly affects the autonomy of those  countries  so  there is space  and there is huge demand  for a positive  a sustainable and a values-driven offer  an offer which puts standards  transparency  and partnership first  and global gateway is europe's offer  it will aim to unlock 300 billion euro  for investment right around the world  to speed up the global twin transition  it is about designing projects that  deliver lasting social and economic  benefits for local communities  in a way that also benefits europe and  our own strategic interests around the  world  so this is not just about developing  cloud and data infrastructure or  building renewable energy capacity it's  also about that  but it is also about ensuring that  people can make the most of the benefits  this can bring  so the ambassadors  when we look at today's world  we see just how many  groundbreaking inventions we have  witnessed in the last years from for  example 5g or artificial intelligence  to solar power clean transport smart  grid technologies you name it  this has improved the way we do things  across europe  and in most major economies  but if we look at the world  the benefits  of these innovations are not felt by a  large proportion of the global  population  so i believe  that the greatest innovations of the  21st century will be those  which ensure that new innovations  can be used and benefited by all  and this will not only require  investment and infrastructure  and stronger supply chains  but also in people in skills in  knowledge  and in the capacity to ensure that they  can be used and operated  and this is where i believe europe and  global gateway have a competitive  advantage  thanks to our world-class researchers  industry and public and private  innovation capacity  and  thanks to your role  on the ground  this will be absolutely central to  global gateway's ability to bring all of  these elements together  we need you to work with our partners  to really identify investment needs and  concrete projects  and to work with member states embassies  to ensure we take a team europe approach  to this fantastic challenge  the ambassador's  wizard is on health infrastructure  development  climate change or digitalization all  topics  i was briefly touching  the world needs to work together to get  things done  there have been many successes in the  last year  by the way not at least the historic  agreement signed by around about 130  countries to make the global tax system  fairer  but we should also not shy away from  where there have also been difficult  moments for global cooperation  which have a profound impact on our  union  this only reinforces the need for europe  to focus on making itself stronger  both to be a better partner but also to  be able to better protect our own  interests and values  this is why we have stepped up our own  work to give ourselves the instruments  to do that  we will soon present a new tool  to dissuade others from using coercion  tactics against us  this tool will equip us with the  necessity to take trade investment or  other restrictive measures  towards those putting undue pressure on  us  we are also strengthening our  partnership with nato on security and  defense  i recently traveled to the baltics with  secretary general jens stoltenberg  and we are working closely on an eu nato  joint declaration  but it is not a new assessment  that europe can and clearly should also  be able and willing to do more on its  own  this will help us provide stability in  our own region and beyond  to better prepare for new threats  and to ensure that we make the most of  our unique combination of strength when  we need to act  so this will be a core theme of our work  in the year ahead  and it shows that europe needs to draw  on its own strength and work closely  with our allies and partners all across  the world  so we will continue to work on all our  partnerships even the most challenging  or complex ones  because  i think we must never see diplomacy  as an endorsement of the other side  but rather as a way to get things done  and to protect our own interests  this is the skill  which hiv p joseph burrell has in  abundance  and i want to thank him  for his leadership and unwavering  support over the last  year and i want to thank all of you  for doing the same  i very much look forward to seeing you  soon hopefully in person  and now i wish you a peaceful and a  successful end of the year  stay healthy
 

